#document(
  default_font = "Helvetica",
  default_size = pt(11),
  page = { size = "letter", orientation = "portrait" },
  margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) }
)

CHART AXIS FLOOR: a value axis starts at zero unless the values have one sign and span at most a sixth of the largest magnitude, when the axis starts half their span beyond the value nearest zero and a twentieth of it beyond the farthest. A stacked chart is judged by its running totals, and the step follows from the padded span and the length of the axis.

#paragraph[Chart 1: column, values 26, 31, height 162 points.]

#chart(
  kind = "column",
  width = pt(216),
  height = pt(162),
  data = {
    categories = { "A", "B" },
    series = {
      { name = "S1", values = { 26, 31 } }
    }
  },
  legend = false
)

